WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:19.415
I went to 221B Baker Street to call on my friend, Mr.

2
00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:20.236
Sherlock Holmes.

3
00:00:20.796 --> 00:00:23.537
Mr. Holmes rents a three-room flat from Mrs.

4
00:00:23.597 --> 00:00:30.160
Hudson. The study, as Holmes liked to call the large sitting room, was always a bit disorderly.

5
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:36.382
When I arrived, I saw that he was talking with a stout, red-faced gentleman with fiery red hair.

6
00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.482
"So sorry to bother you," I said.

7
00:00:38.502 --> 00:00:41.063
"No bother," said Holmes.

8
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:44.284
"I don't think you could have come at a better time.

9
00:00:44.884 --> 00:00:50.526
Mr. Wilson, here, was explaining the circumstances surrounding a most unusual part-time job.

10
00:00:51.406 --> 00:00:53.166
Mr. Wilson, this is Dr.

11
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:58.168
Watson. He has been my helper and partner in many of my most successful cases."

12
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.923
Mr. Wilson and I greeted each other, and I took a seat near Holmes.

13
00:01:03.524 --> 00:01:09.489
Holmes was sitting with his fingertips together, which is his habit when considering a matter of importance.

14
00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:17.876
"My dear Watson," began Holmes, "I know you share my love of bizarre events, and that you like

15
00:01:17.936 --> 00:01:21.820
to retell the stories of my adventures in exciting ways.

16
00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.102
I think you will find Mr.

17
00:01:24.142 --> 00:01:26.344
Wilson's story quite stimulating."

18
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:33.742
I was indeed intrigued, and I answered, "Your cases are always interesting to me, my dear Holmes."

19
00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:41.805
"Mr. Wilson was telling me his story," continued Holmes, "and, if he would be so kind, I would

20
00:01:41.845 --> 00:01:48.867
like him to begin again—first, to introduce you to the case, and second, so that I may better

21
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:50.508
understand the details.

22
00:01:51.424 --> 00:01:57.687
What I have heard so far suggests that this case may be my most extraordinary one yet."

23
00:01:58.847 --> 00:02:04.629
The stout man puffed with obvious pride at Holmes' words and he pulled from his pocket a dirty,

24
00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:06.070
wrinkled newspaper clipping.

25
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:13.053
As he did this, I took the opportunity to examine the man, in the way I imagined Holmes

26
00:02:13.073 --> 00:02:14.453
had already examined him.

27
00:02:15.474 --> 00:02:17.294
I didn't gain much from my survey.

28
00:02:18.315 --> 00:02:19.315
To my eye, Mr.

29
00:02:19.355 --> 00:02:21.056
Wilson seemed quite commonplace.

30
00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.523
He was overweight, and from his attire, I could tell he was a tradesman.

31
00:02:26.524 --> 00:02:31.808
His clothing was slightly worn, and an ornamental gold chain suggested he carried a watch.

32
00:02:32.789 --> 00:02:36.612
Other than his fiery red hair, I observed nothing remarkable.

33
00:02:37.493 --> 00:02:44.659
Holmes, however, stated, "I can deduce nothing beyond the obvious facts that he has at some time done

34
00:02:44.739 --> 00:02:50.204
manual labor, has been to China, and has done a considerable amount of writing lately."

35
00:02:51.644 --> 00:02:57.007
Mr. Wilson gaped at Holmes in amazement and said, "How in the world did you know all that?

36
00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:00.689
It's true when I was younger, I did manual labor.

37
00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:02.270
I was a ship's carpenter."

38
00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.511
"I knew from your hands.

39
00:03:04.972 --> 00:03:09.234
Your right hand is slightly larger than your left," explained Holmes.

40
00:03:09.254 --> 00:03:10.935
"And China?"

41
00:03:11.615 --> 00:03:12.076
asked Mr.

42
00:03:12.096 --> 00:03:18.920
Wilson. "Well, the tattoo on your right wrist could only have been done in China, and you also

43
00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.822
have a Chinese coin hanging from your watch chain," answered Holmes.

44
00:03:22.842 --> 00:03:24.724
"What about the writing?"

45
00:03:25.424 --> 00:03:25.904
asked Mr.

46
00:03:25.924 --> 00:03:32.069
Wilson. "The right cuff of your coat is worn smooth, but the left cuff is not.

47
00:03:32.809 --> 00:03:37.372
There is a patch over the elbow of your left sleeve, but no patch on your right sleeve.

48
00:03:38.113 --> 00:03:42.916
The combination of these facts leads me to believe that you have done a lot of writing lately,"

49
00:03:43.804 --> 00:03:44.644
explained Holmes.

50
00:03:45.685 --> 00:03:46.485
"Quite so!"

51
00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:48.045
exclaimed Mr.

52
00:03:48.085 --> 00:03:48.986
Wilson, impressed.

53
00:03:49.946 --> 00:03:54.567
"I believe you were about to show us a newspaper advertisement," said Holmes.

54
00:03:54.587 --> 00:03:57.188
"Yes, yes," said Mr.

55
00:03:57.208 --> 00:03:58.468
Wilson. "Here it is."

56
00:03:59.048 --> 00:04:04.650
Below is what Holmes and I read: TO ALL RED-HEADED MEN: The late Mr.

57
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.971
Hopkins has left his fortune to help all red-headed men.

58
00:04:08.911 --> 00:04:10.752
A vacancy has opened in the League.

59
00:04:11.304 --> 00:04:13.965
Members can earn a salary of four pounds a week.

60
00:04:14.766 --> 00:04:18.607
All red-headed men 21 years old or older are eligible.

61
00:04:19.568 --> 00:04:25.710
Apply in person on Monday at eleven o'clock to Duncan Ross at the League's office, 7 Pope's Court.

62
00:04:26.991 --> 00:04:30.973
I read it again and exclaimed, "What on earth does this mean?"

63
00:04:31.953 --> 00:04:38.416
Holmes chuckled and said, "Yes, my dear Watson, it's a little off the beaten track, isn't it?"

64
00:04:39.648 --> 00:04:41.069
Holmes then turned to Mr.

65
00:04:41.089 --> 00:04:48.252
Wilson and said, "Please, tell us about your household, your occupation, and the effect this advertisement has had

66
00:04:48.312 --> 00:04:48.872
on your life."

67
00:04:49.952 --> 00:04:53.314
"Well, this whole affair began about two months ago," began Mr.

68
00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:58.016
Wilson. "As I told you, I own a small pawnshop in Coburg Square.

69
00:04:58.776 --> 00:05:01.277
It provides me enough to live on, but nothing more.

70
00:05:02.018 --> 00:05:06.680
I have recently hired a new assistant who agreed to work for half wages so that he could

71
00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.400
learn the business."

72
00:05:08.384 --> 00:05:10.225
"What is the name of this kind youth?"

73
00:05:10.905 --> 00:05:11.385
asked Holmes.

74
00:05:11.405 --> 00:05:16.767
"His name is Vincent Spaulding, although he's not much of a youth," answered Mr.

75
00:05:16.807 --> 00:05:20.428
Wilson. "But I couldn't ask for a smarter assistant.

76
00:05:20.888 --> 00:05:25.710
He could easily earn twice what I pay him, but since he is satisfied, there is no sense

77
00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.451
in putting ideas into his head."

78
00:05:28.331 --> 00:05:30.812
"Yes," said Holmes in agreement.

79
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.481
"You seem most fortunate.

80
00:05:33.921 --> 00:05:38.482
It's hard to get good employees these days, and you have found one for half price.

81
00:05:39.522 --> 00:05:44.644
I think your assistant is almost as interesting as your position at the Red-Headed League."

82
00:05:44.664 --> 00:05:47.885
"Oh, he has his faults," professed Mr.

83
00:05:47.905 --> 00:05:49.745
Wilson. "Really?"

84
00:05:50.405 --> 00:05:51.446
said Holmes curiously.

85
00:05:51.466 --> 00:05:52.986
"Oh yes.

86
00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.927
He is crazy about photography.

87
00:05:55.407 --> 00:06:00.673
He is always taking pictures and then running down to the cellar to develop them, but besides that

88
00:06:00.753 --> 00:06:01.934
he is an excellent worker."

89
00:06:01.954 --> 00:06:03.995
"Is he still with you?"

90
00:06:04.876 --> 00:06:05.356
asked Holmes.

91
00:06:05.376 --> 00:06:10.379
"Yes, he is, and I also have a young girl who does the cooking and cleaning for me.

92
00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.980
There's just the three of us."

93
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.023
"Do you often read the advertisements in the newspaper, Mr.

94
00:06:16.043 --> 00:06:17.684
Wilson?" asked Holmes.

95
00:06:17.704 --> 00:06:19.986
"No, sir," said Mr.

96
00:06:20.006 --> 00:06:22.207
Wilson. "I usually have no need."

97
00:06:22.227 --> 00:06:25.790
"Then may I ask how you learned about this one?"

98
00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:29.032
"My assistant brought it to my attention eight weeks ago.

99
00:06:29.716 --> 00:06:33.679
He came running out of his office saying, 'I wish I were a red-headed man.

100
00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.341
There's a vacancy in the League!'"

101
00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.242
"So Mr.

102
00:06:37.302 --> 00:06:39.104
Spaulding informed you of the opening?"

103
00:06:39.764 --> 00:06:40.265
asked Holmes.

104
00:06:40.285 --> 00:06:43.027
"Yes, exactly," said Mr.

105
00:06:43.047 --> 00:06:45.189
Wilson, "and I looked at Mr.

106
00:06:45.229 --> 00:06:47.991
Spaulding and said, 'What's this nonsense?'

107
00:06:48.652 --> 00:06:52.074
and he replied, 'If I had red hair like you, Mr.

108
00:06:52.094 --> 00:06:55.817
Wilson, I could have a part-time job that earns me four pounds a week.'

109
00:06:55.837 --> 00:06:58.600
'Ridiculous,' I said.

110
00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.421
'Haven't you heard of the Red-Headed League?'

111
00:07:01.661 --> 00:07:02.101
he asked.

112
00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.882
'You, yourself, are eligible,' he said.

113
00:07:05.743 --> 00:07:06.203
Now, Mr.

114
00:07:06.243 --> 00:07:12.165
Holmes, my business isn't doing well, so I was interested in earning a little extra money, but the

115
00:07:12.285 --> 00:07:15.727
idea of getting a job because my hair is red seemed absurd."

116
00:07:15.747 --> 00:07:19.168
"You were skeptical about the advertisement, then?"

117
00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:20.388
asked Holmes.

118
00:07:20.408 --> 00:07:23.049
"Oh yes," replied Mr.

119
00:07:23.069 --> 00:07:24.830
Wilson. "But Mr.

120
00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.091
Spaulding convinced me.

121
00:07:26.551 --> 00:07:28.932
He seemed quite certain that I would get the job.

122
00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.407
He even went with me to the League's office the next day."
